      "latin": "plūrālis, plūrāle",
      "status": "recommended",
      "period": "classical",
      "gloss": "plural, of more than one",
      "evidence": [
        "Quint. 1.5.42: <span lang=\"la\">in quibus nōs singulārem ac plūrālem habēmus</span>",
        "Quint. 1.6.26 (Lewis &amp; Short)",
        "Traupman 221, 248"
      ],
      "comment": "<span lang=\"la\">numerus plūrālis</span>, the plural number; adverb <span lang=\"la\">plūrāliter</span>, in the plural (Sen. NQ 2.56.1; Quint. 1.6.25). Traupman also gives <span lang=\"la\">multitūdō</span> for “a plural”, from his pupil’s <span lang=\"la\">multitūdinem significāns</span>, meaning a plural (248, 221)."
    },
    {
      "latin": "numerus plūrālis",
      "status": "alternative",
      "period": "classical",
      "evidence": [
        "Quint. 1.5.42: <span lang=\"la\">numerōs, in quibus nōs singulārem ac plūrālem habēmus</span> (Lewis &amp; Short)",
        "Traupman 361"
      ],
      "comment": "The number as a whole, in Quintilian; “in the plural” is <span lang=\"la\">plūrāliter</span>."
    },
    {
      "latin": "multitūdō, multitūdinis f.",
      "status": "alternative",
      "period": "classical",
      "gloss": "the plural (number)",
      "evidence": [
        "Varr. LL 9.63 (Lewis &amp; Short s.v. <span lang=\"la\">multitūdō</span>)",
        "Gell. 19.8.13: <span lang=\"la\">numerum multitūdinis capiunt</span> (Lewis &amp; Short)",
        "Traupman 361"
      ],
      "comment": "The older grammatical term, <span lang=\"la\">numerus multitūdinis</span>, or simply <span lang=\"la\">multitūdō</span>."
    }
  ],
